{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"JLSEC-2026-941","published":"2026-07-30T16:02:27.435Z","modified":"2026-07-30T18:35:41.864930969Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-25576","EUVD-2026-7454","GHSA-jv4p-gjwq-9r2j"],"summary":"ImageMagick: Out of bounds read in multiple coders read raw pixel data","details":"ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40, a heap buffer over-read vulnerability exists in multiple raw image format handles. The vulnerability occurs when processing images with -extract dimensions larger than -size dimensions, causing out-of-bounds memory reads from a heap-allocated buffer. Versions 7.1.2-15 and 6.9.13-40 contain a patch.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/ImageMagick_jll?uuid=c73af94c-d91f-53ed-93a7-00f77d67a9d7"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2023+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-941.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/077b42643212d7da8c1a4f6b2cd0067ebca8ec0f"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-jv4p-gjwq-9r2j"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jv4p-gjwq-9r2j"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/dlemstra/Magick.NET/releases/tag/14.10.3"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-25576"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"database_specific":{"status":"Analyzed"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-25576","id":"CVE-2026-25576","imported":"2026-07-30T14:08:44.816Z","modified":"2026-06-17T10:24:53.210Z","published":"2026-02-24T01:16:13.290Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-25576"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jv4p-gjwq-9r2j","id":"GHS